{"module":"movements","voice":"female","duration":469.4,"segments":[{"el":"title","text":"Cómo ganaron los movimientos, y la estrategia para este","start":0.0,"end":3.39,"words":[[0.1,0.36],[0.36,0.81],[0.81,1.0],[1.0,1.77],[2.0,2.06],[2.06,2.19],[2.19,2.84],[2.84,3.09],[3.09,3.35]]},{"el":"intro","text":"El movimiento por los derechos civiles suele recordarse como unos cuantos grandes discursos.","start":4.19,"end":9.54,"words":[[4.27,4.39],[4.39,5.01],[5.01,5.19],[5.19,5.38],[5.38,5.87],[5.87,6.3],[6.3,6.61],[6.61,7.22],[7.22,7.47],[7.47,7.71],[7.71,8.14],[8.14,8.58],[8.58,9.19]]},{"el":"intro","text":"El registro muestra algo más útil: años de preparación, entrenamiento, organización local, demandas judiciales, cabildeo y presión económica, llevados a cabo por miles de personas comunes.","start":9.89,"end":24.44,"words":[[10.0,10.15],[10.15,10.76],[10.76,11.3],[11.3,11.6],[11.6,11.83],[11.83,12.21],[12.48,12.78],[12.78,12.93],[12.93,13.85],[14.11,15.18],[15.44,16.36],[16.36,16.81],[17.08,17.69],[17.69,18.53],[18.79,19.4],[19.4,19.48],[19.48,20.01],[20.01,20.77],[21.04,21.57],[21.57,21.65],[21.65,21.95],[21.95,22.18],[22.18,22.56],[22.56,22.71],[22.71,23.32],[23.32,23.93]]},{"el":"intro","text":"Cada uno de esos métodos puede usarse para aprobar una Ley CAREN federal.","start":24.79,"end":29.33,"words":[[24.85,25.12],[25.12,25.32],[25.32,25.45],[25.45,25.72],[25.72,26.19],[26.19,26.53],[26.53,26.93],[26.93,27.2],[27.2,27.67],[27.67,27.87],[27.87,28.07],[28.07,28.41],[28.41,28.94]]},{"el":"h0","text":"Montgomery: primero la preparación, luego la presión","start":29.68,"end":33.31,"words":[[29.76,30.49],[30.72,31.18],[31.18,31.31],[31.31,32.1],[32.34,32.67],[32.67,32.8],[32.8,33.26]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Rosa Parks no estaba simplemente cansada cuando se negó a ceder su asiento el 1 de diciembre de 1955.","start":34.01,"end":41.58,"words":[[34.08,34.34],[34.34,34.67],[34.67,34.79],[34.79,35.18],[35.18,35.9],[35.9,36.35],[36.35,36.74],[36.74,36.87],[36.87,37.12],[37.12,37.19],[37.19,37.51],[37.51,37.64],[37.64,38.1],[38.1,38.23],[38.23,38.42],[38.42,38.55],[38.55,39.13],[39.13,39.26],[39.26,41.2]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Era la secretaria de la NAACP local y ese verano se había capacitado en organización comunitaria en la Highlander Folk School.","start":41.93,"end":49.58,"words":[[42.03,42.24],[42.24,42.38],[42.38,43.06],[43.06,43.2],[43.2,43.34],[43.34,43.68],[43.68,44.03],[44.03,44.09],[44.09,44.3],[44.3,44.71],[44.71,44.85],[44.85,45.19],[45.19,45.88],[45.88,46.02],[46.02,46.84],[46.84,47.6],[47.6,47.74],[47.74,47.88],[47.88,48.43],[48.43,48.7],[48.7,49.18]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Jo Ann Robinson y el Consejo Político de Mujeres llevaban meses planeando un boicot; imprimieron decenas de miles de volantes en una sola noche.","start":49.93,"end":60.22,"words":[[50.02,50.18],[50.18,50.42],[50.42,51.05],[51.05,51.13],[51.13,51.28],[51.28,51.83],[51.83,52.46],[52.46,52.62],[52.62,53.17],[53.17,53.72],[53.72,54.12],[54.12,54.83],[54.83,54.98],[54.98,55.53],[55.81,56.68],[56.68,57.23],[57.23,57.38],[57.38,57.78],[57.78,57.94],[57.94,58.57],[58.57,58.72],[58.72,58.96],[58.96,59.27],[59.27,59.75]]},{"el":"s0","text":"El boicot duró 381 días, sostenido por un sistema de viajes compartidos que movía a miles de personas al día.","start":60.57,"end":68.78,"words":[[60.66,60.79],[60.79,61.2],[61.2,61.46],[61.46,63.0],[63.0,63.4],[63.64,64.24],[64.24,64.44],[64.44,64.57],[64.57,65.04],[65.04,65.18],[65.18,65.58],[65.58,66.31],[66.31,66.45],[66.45,66.85],[66.85,66.92],[66.92,67.25],[67.25,67.38],[67.38,67.92],[67.92,68.05],[68.05,68.39]]},{"el":"s0","text":"Lo que finalmente puso fin a la segregación en los autobuses fue una demanda, Browder v. Gayle, que la Corte Suprema confirmó en noviembre de 1956.","start":69.13,"end":80.25,"words":[[69.21,69.34],[69.34,69.48],[69.48,70.16],[70.16,70.43],[70.43,70.63],[70.63,70.7],[70.7,70.84],[70.84,71.59],[71.59,71.72],[71.72,71.93],[71.93,72.54],[72.54,72.74],[72.74,72.94],[72.94,73.49],[73.73,74.2],[74.2,74.41],[74.74,75.15],[75.39,75.53],[75.53,75.66],[75.66,76.0],[76.0,76.48],[76.48,77.02],[77.02,77.16],[77.16,77.77],[77.77,77.9],[77.9,79.87]]},{"el":"s0","text":"El boicot mantuvo la presión y a la comunidad unida mientras el caso avanzaba en los tribunales.","start":80.6,"end":86.92,"words":[[80.68,80.83],[80.83,81.26],[81.26,81.77],[81.77,81.92],[81.92,82.43],[82.43,82.5],[82.5,82.57],[82.57,82.72],[82.72,83.37],[83.37,83.74],[83.74,84.32],[84.32,84.46],[84.46,84.76],[84.76,85.34],[85.34,85.48],[85.48,85.7],[85.7,86.5]]},{"el":"h1","text":"Brown v. Board: una estrategia legal de 20 años","start":87.82,"end":91.72,"words":[[87.9,88.25],[88.25,88.47],[88.83,89.26],[89.51,89.72],[89.72,90.44],[90.44,90.8],[90.8,90.94],[90.94,91.37],[91.37,91.66]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Los abogados de la NAACP no empezaron por las escuelas primarias.","start":92.42,"end":96.32,"words":[[92.54,92.72],[92.72,93.22],[93.22,93.35],[93.35,93.47],[93.47,93.78],[93.78,93.91],[93.91,94.47],[94.47,94.65],[94.65,94.84],[94.84,95.34],[95.34,95.96]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Charles Hamilton Houston y su alumno Thurgood Marshall atacaron primero las escuelas de posgrado y de derecho segregadas, donde la desigualdad era más fácil de probar: Murray v. Pearson (1936), Gaines (1938), Sweatt v. Painter (1950).","start":96.67,"end":115.63,"words":[[96.72,97.19],[97.19,97.65],[97.65,98.06],[98.06,98.12],[98.12,98.26],[98.26,98.66],[98.66,99.12],[99.12,99.53],[99.53,100.06],[100.06,100.53],[100.53,100.73],[100.73,101.26],[101.26,101.4],[101.4,101.93],[101.93,102.0],[102.0,102.13],[102.13,102.6],[102.6,103.33],[103.57,103.9],[103.9,104.04],[104.04,104.77],[104.77,104.97],[104.97,105.17],[105.17,105.51],[105.51,105.64],[105.64,106.11],[106.34,106.68],[106.68,106.88],[107.21,107.68],[107.68,109.48],[109.72,110.12],[110.12,111.99],[112.22,112.62],[112.62,112.83],[113.16,113.63],[113.63,115.23]]},{"el":"s1","text":"Cada victoria sentó un precedente hasta que, en 1954, Brown v. Board of Education anuló el principio de “separados pero iguales”.","start":115.98,"end":126.9,"words":[[116.03,116.32],[116.32,116.89],[116.89,117.25],[117.25,117.4],[117.4,118.12],[118.12,118.41],[118.41,118.62],[118.87,119.02],[119.02,121.25],[121.5,121.86],[121.86,122.08],[122.44,122.8],[122.8,122.94],[122.94,123.59],[123.59,123.95],[123.95,124.1],[124.1,124.75],[124.75,124.89],[124.89,125.54],[125.54,125.83],[125.83,126.4]]},{"el":"h2","text":"Las sentadas: entrenamiento y disciplina","start":127.8,"end":131.03,"words":[[127.93,128.17],[128.17,128.88],[129.16,130.19],[130.19,130.27],[130.27,130.99]]},{"el":"s2","text":"El 1 de febrero de 1960, cuatro estudiantes de North Carolina A&T se sentaron en la barra de un Woolworth's de Greensboro reservada para blancos.","start":131.73,"end":141.35,"words":[[131.83,131.96],[131.96,132.15],[132.15,132.28],[132.28,132.74],[132.74,132.87],[132.87,134.3],[134.53,134.92],[134.92,135.63],[135.63,135.76],[135.76,136.02],[136.02,136.54],[136.54,136.8],[136.8,136.93],[136.93,137.45],[137.45,137.58],[137.58,137.71],[137.71,137.97],[137.97,138.1],[138.1,138.23],[138.23,138.82],[138.82,138.95],[138.95,139.6],[139.6,140.18],[140.18,140.44],[140.44,140.96]]},{"el":"s2","text":"En pocas semanas, las sentadas se extendieron a decenas de ciudades.","start":141.7,"end":146.34,"words":[[141.77,141.91],[141.91,142.23],[142.23,142.75],[142.98,143.18],[143.18,143.7],[143.7,143.83],[143.83,144.62],[144.62,144.68],[144.68,145.14],[145.14,145.27],[145.27,145.86]]},{"el":"s2","text":"En Nashville, los estudiantes se entrenaron durante meses en los talleres de no violencia de James Lawson, ensayando cómo aguantar insultos y golpes sin devolverlos.","start":146.69,"end":157.12,"words":[[146.82,146.95],[146.95,147.56],[147.8,148.0],[148.0,148.74],[148.74,148.88],[148.88,149.55],[149.55,150.02],[150.02,150.36],[150.36,150.49],[150.49,150.7],[150.7,151.24],[151.24,151.37],[151.37,151.51],[151.51,152.11],[152.11,152.25],[152.25,152.59],[152.59,153.06],[153.29,153.9],[153.9,154.17],[154.17,154.71],[154.71,155.25],[155.25,155.32],[155.32,155.72],[155.72,155.93],[155.93,156.74]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Junto con un boicot al centro de la ciudad, lograron que las barras se desegregaran en mayo.","start":157.47,"end":163.09,"words":[[157.55,157.89],[157.89,158.09],[158.09,158.22],[158.22,158.62],[158.62,158.76],[158.76,159.16],[159.16,159.29],[159.29,159.42],[159.42,159.89],[160.12,160.66],[160.66,160.79],[160.79,160.99],[160.99,161.33],[161.33,161.46],[161.46,162.26],[162.26,162.39],[162.39,162.73]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Ese abril, Ella Baker ayudó a los estudiantes a fundar el Comité Coordinador Estudiantil No Violento (SNCC).","start":163.44,"end":170.03,"words":[[163.55,163.74],[163.74,164.11],[164.32,164.57],[164.57,164.88],[164.88,165.18],[165.18,165.24],[165.24,165.43],[165.43,166.11],[166.11,166.17],[166.17,166.54],[166.54,166.66],[166.66,167.03],[167.03,167.7],[167.7,168.38],[168.38,168.5],[168.5,169.0],[169.0,169.67]]},{"el":"s2","text":"Su principio: “La gente fuerte no necesita líderes fuertes”.","start":170.38,"end":174.47,"words":[[170.44,170.57],[170.57,171.26],[171.49,171.63],[171.63,171.97],[171.97,172.38],[172.38,172.52],[172.52,173.06],[173.06,173.54],[173.54,174.09]]},{"el":"h3","text":"De Birmingham a la Ley de Derechos Civiles: crisis, coalición, cabildeo","start":175.37,"end":180.56,"words":[[175.44,175.59],[175.59,176.24],[176.24,176.31],[176.31,176.45],[176.45,176.67],[176.67,176.81],[176.81,177.39],[177.39,177.97],[178.22,178.72],[178.97,179.69],[179.95,180.52]]},{"el":"s3","text":"En la primavera de 1963, los organizadores de Birmingham combinaron marchas, un boicot a las tiendas del centro y la Cruzada de los Niños.","start":181.26,"end":191.32,"words":[[181.37,181.51],[181.51,181.64],[181.64,182.24],[182.24,182.38],[182.38,184.18],[184.41,184.61],[184.61,185.48],[185.48,185.61],[185.61,186.21],[186.21,186.88],[186.88,187.41],[187.65,187.78],[187.78,188.18],[188.18,188.25],[188.25,188.45],[188.45,188.92],[188.92,189.12],[189.12,189.52],[189.52,189.58],[189.58,189.72],[189.72,190.18],[190.18,190.32],[190.32,190.52],[190.52,190.92]]},{"el":"s3","text":"Las imágenes televisadas de perros policías y mangueras de bomberos contra niños obligaron al país a enfrentar la realidad.","start":191.67,"end":199.19,"words":[[191.74,191.94],[191.94,192.49],[192.49,193.23],[193.23,193.37],[193.37,193.71],[193.71,194.32],[194.32,194.39],[194.39,194.93],[194.93,195.07],[195.07,195.61],[195.61,196.02],[196.02,196.36],[196.36,196.97],[196.97,197.1],[197.1,197.38],[197.38,197.44],[197.44,198.06],[198.06,198.19],[198.19,198.8]]},{"el":"s3","text":"El 11 de junio, el presidente Kennedy propuso una ley de derechos civiles.","start":199.54,"end":204.48,"words":[[199.67,199.8],[199.8,200.07],[200.07,200.2],[200.2,200.59],[200.82,200.95],[200.95,201.61],[201.61,202.07],[202.07,202.53],[202.53,202.72],[202.72,202.92],[202.92,203.05],[203.05,203.58],[203.58,204.1]]},{"el":"s3","text":"La Marcha sobre Washington de ese agosto reunió a unas 250,000 personas.","start":204.83,"end":210.94,"words":[[204.94,205.06],[205.06,205.44],[205.44,205.75],[205.75,206.32],[206.32,206.44],[206.44,206.63],[206.63,207.01],[207.01,207.39],[207.39,207.45],[207.45,207.7],[207.7,209.9],[209.9,210.47]]},{"el":"s3","text":"La ley todavía tenía que pasar por el Congreso.","start":211.29,"end":214.3,"words":[[211.4,211.53],[211.53,211.72],[211.72,212.22],[212.22,212.6],[212.6,212.73],[212.73,213.04],[213.04,213.23],[213.23,213.36],[213.36,213.92]]},{"el":"s3","text":"La Leadership Conference on Civil Rights coordinó a iglesias, sindicatos y grupos cívicos para presionar a cada senador, y el cabildero de la NAACP Clarence Mitchell estaba tan presente que lo llamaban “el senador 101”.","start":214.65,"end":228.18,"words":[[214.74,214.88],[214.88,215.49],[215.49,216.18],[216.18,216.31],[216.31,216.66],[216.66,217.0],[217.0,217.54],[217.54,217.61],[217.61,218.23],[218.47,219.15],[219.15,219.22],[219.22,219.63],[219.63,220.11],[220.11,220.38],[220.38,221.0],[221.0,221.07],[221.07,221.34],[221.34,221.89],[222.13,222.19],[222.19,222.33],[222.33,222.95],[222.95,223.08],[223.08,223.22],[223.22,223.56],[223.56,224.11],[224.11,224.59],[224.59,225.0],[225.0,225.2],[225.2,225.75],[225.75,225.89],[225.89,226.02],[226.02,226.5],[226.5,226.64],[226.64,227.12],[227.12,227.8]]},{"el":"s3","text":"El Senado rompió un obstruccionismo (filibuster) el 10 de junio de 1964, y el presidente Johnson firmó la Ley de Derechos Civiles el 2 de julio.","start":228.53,"end":239.01,"words":[[228.62,228.75],[228.75,229.15],[229.15,229.54],[229.54,229.68],[229.68,230.67],[230.67,231.33],[231.57,231.7],[231.7,231.96],[231.96,232.1],[232.1,232.43],[232.43,232.56],[232.56,234.48],[234.71,234.78],[234.78,234.91],[234.91,235.57],[235.57,235.97],[235.97,236.3],[236.3,236.44],[236.44,236.63],[236.63,236.77],[236.77,237.3],[237.3,237.76],[237.76,237.89],[237.89,238.09],[238.09,238.22],[238.22,238.62]]},{"el":"h4","text":"Selma: primero, años de organización local","start":239.91,"end":243.52,"words":[[240.0,240.47],[240.75,241.38],[241.66,241.97],[241.97,242.13],[242.13,243.08],[243.08,243.47]]},{"el":"s4","text":"El Domingo Sangriento de 1965 pareció repentino.","start":244.22,"end":248.78,"words":[[244.3,244.43],[244.43,244.86],[244.86,245.55],[245.55,245.68],[245.68,247.37],[247.37,247.8],[247.8,248.43]]},{"el":"s4","text":"No lo fue.","start":249.13,"end":249.91,"words":[[249.2,249.3],[249.3,249.4],[249.4,249.6]]},{"el":"s4","text":"Los organizadores del SNCC trabajaban en Selma desde 1963, con campañas de registro de votantes y ganándose la confianza familia por familia.","start":250.26,"end":260.64,"words":[[250.35,250.55],[250.55,251.4],[251.4,251.59],[251.59,252.25],[252.25,252.9],[252.9,253.03],[253.03,253.36],[253.36,253.69],[253.69,255.45],[255.68,255.87],[255.87,256.4],[256.4,256.53],[256.53,257.05],[257.05,257.18],[257.18,257.7],[257.7,257.77],[257.77,258.36],[258.36,258.49],[258.49,259.08],[259.08,259.53],[259.53,259.73],[259.73,260.25]]},{"el":"s4","text":"El Verano de la Libertad de 1964 llevó a Misisipi a unos 1,000 voluntarios, la mayoría estudiantes universitarios blancos, y el Partido Demócrata por la Libertad de Misisipi de Fannie Lou Hamer desafió a la delegación totalmente blanca en la convención demócrata de 1964 ante la televisión nacional.","start":260.99,"end":284.04,"words":[[261.08,261.22],[261.22,261.65],[261.65,261.79],[261.79,261.93],[261.93,262.49],[262.49,262.63],[262.63,264.6],[264.6,264.89],[264.89,264.96],[264.96,265.52],[265.52,265.59],[265.59,265.87],[265.87,267.21],[267.21,268.06],[268.3,268.44],[268.44,269.01],[269.01,269.78],[269.78,270.77],[270.77,271.33],[271.58,271.65],[271.65,271.79],[271.79,272.28],[272.28,272.92],[272.92,273.13],[273.13,273.27],[273.27,273.83],[273.83,273.97],[273.97,274.54],[274.54,274.68],[274.68,275.1],[275.1,275.31],[275.31,275.6],[275.6,276.09],[276.09,276.16],[276.16,276.3],[276.3,277.0],[277.0,277.71],[277.71,278.13],[278.13,278.27],[278.27,278.41],[278.41,279.12],[279.12,279.75],[279.75,279.89],[279.89,281.87],[281.87,282.15],[282.15,282.29],[282.29,282.99],[282.99,283.63]]},{"el":"s4","text":"(Ver el módulo sobre el voto.)","start":284.39,"end":286.25,"words":[[284.48,284.67],[284.67,284.8],[284.8,285.19],[285.19,285.51],[285.51,285.64],[285.64,285.97]]},{"el":"h5","text":"¿La disrupción ayuda o perjudica?","start":287.15,"end":289.41,"words":[[287.28,287.41],[287.41,288.04],[288.04,288.35],[288.35,288.41],[288.41,289.04]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Historiadores y politólogos todavía discuten qué tácticas cambiaron la opinión pública.","start":290.11,"end":295.51,"words":[[290.17,290.95],[290.95,291.01],[291.01,291.73],[291.73,292.25],[292.25,292.77],[292.77,292.9],[292.9,293.42],[293.42,294.01],[294.01,294.14],[294.14,294.59],[294.59,295.11]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Un estudio de 2020 de Omar Wasow encontró que las protestas no violentas de los años 60 aumentaron el apoyo a los derechos civiles, mientras que las que se volvieron violentas empujaron a algunos votantes blancos hacia candidatos de “ley y orden” en 1968.","start":295.86,"end":312.58,"words":[[295.95,296.08],[296.08,296.54],[296.54,296.68],[296.68,297.47],[297.47,297.6],[297.6,297.87],[297.87,298.2],[298.2,298.73],[298.73,298.86],[298.86,299.06],[299.06,299.66],[299.66,299.79],[299.79,300.39],[300.39,300.52],[300.52,300.72],[300.72,300.98],[300.98,301.45],[301.45,302.11],[302.11,302.24],[302.24,302.57],[302.57,302.64],[302.64,302.84],[302.84,303.37],[303.37,303.9],[304.13,304.66],[304.66,304.79],[304.79,304.99],[304.99,305.12],[305.12,305.25],[305.25,305.85],[305.85,306.45],[306.45,307.04],[307.04,307.11],[307.11,307.57],[307.57,308.1],[308.1,308.57],[308.57,308.83],[308.83,309.49],[309.49,309.63],[309.63,309.82],[309.82,309.89],[309.89,310.22],[310.22,310.35],[310.35,312.21]]},{"el":"s5","text":"Otros sostienen que la amenaza de grupos más militantes y de la autodefensa armada (como los Deacons for Defense) hizo que las autoridades estuvieran más dispuestas a negociar con los líderes no violentos.","start":312.93,"end":325.22,"words":[[313.01,313.35],[313.35,313.97],[313.97,314.11],[314.11,314.25],[314.25,314.73],[314.73,314.87],[314.87,315.28],[315.28,315.49],[315.49,316.18],[316.18,316.25],[316.25,316.39],[316.39,316.53],[316.53,317.29],[317.29,317.7],[317.7,317.98],[317.98,318.18],[318.18,318.67],[318.67,318.87],[318.87,319.36],[319.6,319.8],[319.8,319.94],[319.94,320.15],[320.15,320.91],[320.91,321.6],[321.6,321.81],[321.81,322.5],[322.5,322.57],[322.57,323.12],[323.12,323.32],[323.32,323.53],[323.53,324.02],[324.02,324.15],[324.15,324.84]]},{"el":"s5","text":"La mayoría coincide en que la disciplina, las demandas claras y una amplia simpatía pública fueron esenciales.","start":325.57,"end":333.61,"words":[[325.66,325.81],[325.81,326.42],[326.42,327.03],[327.03,327.18],[327.18,327.34],[327.34,327.49],[327.49,328.25],[328.52,328.75],[328.75,329.35],[329.35,329.81],[329.81,329.89],[329.89,330.12],[330.12,330.65],[330.65,331.33],[331.33,331.87],[331.87,332.32],[332.32,333.16]]},{"el":"h6","text":"Victorias recientes que esta campaña puede copiar","start":334.51,"end":337.67,"words":[[334.59,335.24],[335.24,335.89],[335.89,336.03],[336.03,336.32],[336.32,336.82],[336.82,337.18],[337.18,337.62]]},{"el":"s6","text":"La Ley CAREN de San Francisco pasó de su presentación a un voto unánime en unos tres meses en 2020.","start":338.37,"end":344.97,"words":[[338.46,338.6],[338.6,338.81],[338.81,339.16],[339.16,339.3],[339.3,339.51],[339.51,340.13],[340.13,340.41],[340.41,340.55],[340.55,340.69],[340.69,341.52],[341.52,341.59],[341.59,341.73],[341.73,342.0],[342.0,342.49],[342.49,342.63],[342.63,342.91],[342.91,343.18],[343.18,343.53],[343.53,343.67],[343.67,344.57]]},{"el":"s6","text":"La ley de Oregón se aprobó en 2019 porque una legisladora estatal, Janelle Bynum, sufrió una llamada a la policía mientras hacía campaña puerta a puerta y contó su historia.","start":345.32,"end":357.81,"words":[[345.42,345.57],[345.57,345.79],[345.79,345.94],[345.94,346.38],[346.38,346.53],[346.53,346.97],[346.97,347.12],[347.12,348.3],[348.3,348.67],[348.67,348.89],[348.89,349.7],[349.7,350.29],[350.55,351.07],[351.07,351.51],[351.77,352.29],[352.29,352.51],[352.51,352.95],[352.95,353.03],[353.03,353.17],[353.17,353.76],[353.76,354.35],[354.35,354.72],[354.72,355.24],[355.24,355.68],[355.68,355.76],[355.76,356.2],[356.2,356.27],[356.27,356.64],[356.64,356.79],[356.79,357.38]]},{"el":"s6","text":"La campaña “Ban the box” se extendió ciudad por ciudad antes de que los estados la adoptaran.","start":358.16,"end":363.73,"words":[[358.27,358.41],[358.41,358.88],[358.88,359.08],[359.08,359.22],[359.22,359.49],[359.49,359.62],[359.62,360.23],[360.23,360.63],[360.63,360.84],[360.84,361.24],[361.24,361.58],[361.58,361.71],[361.71,361.85],[361.85,362.05],[362.05,362.52],[362.52,362.66],[362.66,363.33]]},{"el":"s6","text":"En 2018, los votantes de Florida devolvieron el derecho al voto a más de un millón de personas mediante una iniciativa ciudadana que obtuvo el 64.6% de los votos.","start":364.08,"end":377.04,"words":[[364.16,364.31],[364.31,365.51],[365.76,365.98],[365.98,366.54],[366.54,366.69],[366.69,367.18],[367.18,367.96],[367.96,368.11],[368.11,368.6],[368.6,368.75],[368.75,369.03],[369.03,369.1],[369.1,369.31],[369.31,369.46],[369.46,369.6],[369.6,370.02],[370.02,370.17],[370.17,370.73],[370.73,371.3],[371.3,371.52],[371.52,372.23],[372.23,372.87],[372.87,373.01],[373.01,373.43],[373.43,373.58],[373.58,375.85],[375.85,375.99],[375.99,376.2],[376.2,376.63]]},{"el":"s6","text":"El patrón: empezar en lo local, contar historias reales y luego llevarlo al estado y al país.","start":377.39,"end":384.36,"words":[[377.51,377.67],[377.67,378.21],[378.49,379.03],[379.03,379.19],[379.19,379.35],[379.35,379.81],[380.09,380.56],[380.56,381.18],[381.18,381.65],[381.65,381.73],[381.73,382.12],[382.12,382.67],[382.67,382.82],[382.82,383.29],[383.29,383.37],[383.37,383.52],[383.52,383.91]]},{"el":"h7","text":"La estrategia para una Ley CAREN federal","start":385.26,"end":387.8,"words":[[385.35,385.49],[385.49,386.2],[386.2,386.48],[386.48,386.7],[386.7,386.91],[386.91,387.26],[387.26,387.76]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Mapea el poder.","start":388.5,"end":390.07,"words":[[388.58,388.98],[388.98,389.13],[389.13,389.61]]},{"el":"s7","text":"¿Quién decide?","start":390.42,"end":391.4,"words":[[390.49,390.7],[390.7,391.08]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Los Comités Judiciales de la Cámara y el Senado estudian el proyecto; tus propios miembros lo votan.","start":391.75,"end":398.07,"words":[[391.85,392.05],[392.05,392.52],[392.52,393.19],[393.19,393.32],[393.32,393.45],[393.45,393.85],[393.85,393.92],[393.92,394.05],[394.05,394.45],[394.45,394.99],[394.99,395.12],[395.12,395.72],[395.95,396.15],[396.15,396.62],[396.62,397.15],[397.15,397.29],[397.29,397.69]]},{"el":"s7","text":"La capa de aliados del mapa los muestra.","start":398.42,"end":400.99,"words":[[398.54,398.66],[398.66,398.91],[398.91,399.03],[399.03,399.46],[399.46,399.64],[399.64,399.89],[399.89,400.07],[400.07,400.56]]},{"el":"s7","text":"(Misión: Mapea quién decide.)","start":401.34,"end":403.63,"words":[[401.46,401.95],[402.2,402.55],[402.55,402.84],[402.84,403.33]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Gana primero en lo local.","start":403.98,"end":405.66,"words":[[404.09,404.32],[404.32,404.73],[404.73,404.84],[404.84,404.96],[404.96,405.3]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Las resoluciones de concejos municipales y las leyes estatales sientan precedentes y le muestran al Congreso una ola.","start":406.01,"end":413.9,"words":[[406.12,406.34],[406.34,407.22],[407.22,407.37],[407.37,407.96],[407.96,408.77],[408.77,408.84],[408.84,409.06],[409.06,409.43],[409.43,410.09],[410.09,410.61],[410.61,411.42],[411.42,411.49],[411.49,411.64],[411.64,412.23],[412.23,412.38],[412.38,412.96],[412.96,413.19],[413.19,413.48]]},{"el":"s7","text":"(Misión: Gana una resolución local.)","start":414.25,"end":417.07,"words":[[414.37,414.87],[415.12,415.41],[415.41,415.63],[415.63,416.34],[416.34,416.77]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Construye una coalición inesperada.","start":417.42,"end":419.71,"words":[[417.5,418.03],[418.03,418.2],[418.2,418.73],[418.73,419.37]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Iglesias, sindicatos, grupos de derechos civiles, grupos asiático-americanos, latinos e indígenas, y negocios que no quieren que acosen a sus clientes.","start":420.06,"end":430.3,"words":[[420.16,420.76],[421.0,421.73],[421.97,422.37],[422.37,422.5],[422.5,423.04],[423.04,423.57],[423.81,424.21],[424.21,425.48],[425.72,426.19],[426.19,426.25],[426.25,426.92],[427.16,427.22],[427.22,427.76],[427.76,427.89],[427.89,428.03],[428.03,428.43],[428.43,428.56],[428.56,428.96],[428.96,429.03],[429.03,429.23],[429.23,429.9]]},{"el":"s7","text":"(Misión: Construye una coalición.)","start":430.65,"end":432.99,"words":[[430.76,431.19],[431.4,431.95],[431.95,432.14],[432.14,432.75]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Cuenta historias respaldadas por datos.","start":433.34,"end":435.83,"words":[[433.44,433.8],[433.8,434.28],[434.28,434.94],[434.94,435.12],[435.12,435.48]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Las historias personales mueven a los legisladores; los datos de resultados del 911 y de la BJS protegen esas historias para que no las descarten.","start":436.18,"end":446.13,"words":[[436.31,436.51],[436.51,437.05],[437.05,437.72],[437.72,438.12],[438.12,438.19],[438.19,438.39],[438.39,439.26],[439.5,439.7],[439.7,440.03],[440.03,440.17],[440.17,440.84],[440.84,441.04],[441.04,442.05],[442.05,442.12],[442.12,442.25],[442.25,442.38],[442.38,442.99],[442.99,443.53],[443.53,443.79],[443.79,444.33],[444.33,444.6],[444.6,444.73],[444.73,444.87],[444.87,445.07],[445.07,445.74]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Trabaja adentro y afuera a la vez.","start":446.48,"end":448.92,"words":[[446.57,447.04],[447.04,447.52],[447.52,447.58],[447.58,447.99],[447.99,448.06],[448.06,448.19],[448.19,448.46]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Reuniones con el personal y testimonios en audiencias, más presión pública: llamadas, columnas de opinión, eventos.","start":449.27,"end":457.99,"words":[[449.35,450.0],[450.0,450.22],[450.22,450.36],[450.36,450.95],[450.95,451.02],[451.02,451.82],[451.82,451.96],[451.96,452.76],[453.02,453.24],[453.24,453.75],[453.75,454.33],[454.58,455.16],[455.42,456.0],[456.0,456.15],[456.15,456.73],[456.98,457.56]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Capacita a la gente y sigue adelante.","start":458.34,"end":460.9,"words":[[458.42,458.97],[458.97,459.04],[459.04,459.17],[459.17,459.52],[459.52,459.59],[459.59,459.86],[459.86,460.49]]},{"el":"s7","text":"Los talleres convierten a quienes aprenden en organizadores.","start":461.25,"end":464.67,"words":[[461.37,461.54],[461.54,462.0],[462.0,462.57],[462.57,462.62],[462.62,462.96],[462.96,463.42],[463.42,463.53],[463.53,464.33]]},{"el":"s7","text":"La mayoría de las victorias tardan años, no semanas.","start":465.02,"end":468.5,"words":[[465.12,465.25],[465.25,465.75],[465.75,465.87],[465.87,466.06],[466.06,466.62],[466.62,466.99],[466.99,467.3],[467.52,467.64],[467.64,468.14]]}]}